<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>

<!-- The frost bomb under Combat Extended.

     Read this before changing it, because the interesting part is what the file does not do.

     CE turns every hand grenade into ammo. Their patch on the vanilla three sets Class to
     CombatExtended.AmmoDef, thingClass to AmmoThing, a stackLimit of 75, and a verb of
     Verb_ShootCEOneUse - whose SelfConsume() destroys the grenade you just threw and equips the
     next one out of your pack. That is a coherent design and it is not this one. The frost bomb
     is a charge compressor in a throwable tube: it builds the next bomb between throws, which is
     what its six-second cooldown is, and it is reusable with or without CE for the same reason a
     frag grenade is reusable without it. One item, one set of numbers, one paragraph in the
     README, whatever the modlist says.

     So this patch gives the weapon CE's stats and CE's melee tool and stops. It deliberately
     leaves alone:

       - the verb. RimArt.Verb_ThrowFrostBomb hands the launch to MapComponent_Throws so the
         grenade leaves the hand on the tick the throw animation opens it. CE's verb spawns its
         projectile inside TryCastShot, and it casts what it spawns straight to ProjectileCE:

             protected virtual ProjectileCE SpawnProjectile()
                 => (ProjectileCE)ThingMaker.MakeThing(Projectile, null);

         Taking their verb therefore costs both the animation and the projectile class, and the
         animation is the feature. What is given up by keeping ours is CE's ballistic flight
         model for this one lobbed grenade - no height, no cover interception on the way in. On a
         cell-targeted 3.4-cell stun that is a much smaller loss than it would be on a bullet.

       - the projectile, which names Projectile_Explosive itself precisely so that CE's rewrite
         of BaseGrenadeProjectile's thingClass does not reach it. See AG_Frost_Things.xml.

     Nothing here is conditional on anything but the folder: loadFolders.xml only reads this
     directory when CE is active, so every type named below is guaranteed to exist. -->

<Patch>

  <!-- Bulk, which is the stat CE actually plans a pawn's kit around - a colonist can be under
       the weight limit and still unable to move for volume. Priced against their frag grenade at
       0.87: the tube is a little bigger than a frag and a little lighter, being mostly gas. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AG_FrostBomb"]/statBases</xpath>
    <value>
      <Bulk>1.1</Bulk>
      <SightsEfficiency>1.0</SightsEfficiency>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Every weapon in CE needs a ToolCE rather than a vanilla Tool, or a pawn who bashes
       somebody with it goes through a code path that expects CE's armour penetration fields and
       does not find them. Their own grenade patch adds exactly this tool; so does this. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AG_FrostBomb"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <tools>
        <li Class="CombatExtended.ToolCE">
          <label>tube</label>
          <capacities>
            <li>Blunt</li>
          </capacities>
          <power>2</power>
          <cooldownTime>1.75</cooldownTime>
          <armorPenetrationBlunt>1.0</armorPenetrationBlunt>
          <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Base</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        </li>
      </tools>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <!-- CE_OneHandedWeapon so it can be carried alongside a shield, which is the combination the
       item is for: walk somebody up behind a shield, freeze the line, pull the wounded out. The
       CE_AI_* tags are pointedly absent - they are what tells CE's raider generator to hand a
       weapon out, and nothing in this mod is given to raiders. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AG_FrostBomb"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <weaponTags>
        <li>CE_OneHandedWeapon</li>
      </weaponTags>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
